From e668a6baed8d78e73902e4a1a41529bc327e0d85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:25:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] minicargo: git dependencies resolve from the vendor
 directory, packages anywhere in a git checkout count

gdrive 3.9.1 (gdrive3) Cargo.toml:14 `google-drive3 = { git = "https://github.com/prasmussen/google-apis-rs", branch =
"resumable-fix" }`: "EXCEPTION: TODO: Cargo.toml:14: Support git dependencies". minicargo fetches nothing: the
PortGroup's cargo.crates_github extracts GitHub's archive of the commit (the WHOLE repository) into the vendor
directory as `<repo>-<rev>/` and writes `.cargo-checksum.json` with `"package": null`.

manifest: `git`/`branch`/`tag`/`rev` of a dependency are accepted; the URL is kept (has_git() was a `false` stub) and
the dependency loads from the repository like a registry one, with any version when it names none (`version`, if
given, still applies; a dependency with neither version nor path used to be "No source"). In `[patch.<source>]`, git
keys are ignored (the vendored checkout is used) and a `path` patch applies for a git source as for crates-io (it was
ignored).

repository: a vendor entry marked `"package": null` (as the PortGroup and `cargo vendor` write it for git sources), or
whose root manifest has no `[package]` (a bare workspace), is a git checkout: every package in its tree is recorded, as
cargo's git source finds them (no hidden directories, no `target` of a package, depth limit 16). google-drive3 is
`google-apis-rs-<rev>/gen/drive3`; the repository root is a `[workspace]` that excludes `gen`. A package in a checkout
inherits (`version.workspace = true`, `edition.workspace`, `x = { workspace = true }`) from the nearest manifest with
`[workspace]` keys above it in the checkout, not from the project's workspace: when loaded by name and as a path
dependency, and its inherited version is what a `version` requirement is matched against. A registry copy of the same
name and version wins over one inside a checkout; a registry crate's nested packages (`fuzz/`) still don't count. The
top-level scan skips `.` and `..` (`<vendor>/../Cargo.toml` was read as a vendored package).

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context)
